// expect: refused
// why: a generic static takes its type arguments from the slot, so its parameter types come from there too
// spec:  §wac-method-argmatch-9tq4mz2
// from: found probing which positions on a generic were still unchecked after 0201
//
// **`Pending.of` is how every capability answer in this repository is built**, which is what makes this
// worth its own case: a static on a generic is the shape the platform's whole surface is made of, and
// its arguments were the last unchecked position.
//
// The receiver is the bare template — `Box`, not `Box<i32>` — so nothing about it says what `T` is, and
// `issues/lang/0141`'s rule is that the *slot* does. The checker already computed that instantiation
// here, to give a lambda argument its target type; it was giving lambdas a slot and letting every other
// argument through unchecked.
//
// A call with no slot still binds nothing and is still accepted, which is the silence the rest of
// inference keeps rather than an exception carved out for this.

struct Box<T> {
  T v;
  Box<T> of(T v) { return Box<T>(v); }
}

export i32 f() {
  // `expected i32, found string`: the slot says `Box<i32>`, so `of` takes an `i32`.
  Box<i32> b = Box.of("no");
  return b.v;
}
